  data: {
    LLM: 'Players bet; each receives three tiles and arranges them in a line to form top and bottom hand (totals mod 10). Tiles placed face-down. Banker exposes three tiles and arranges similarly. Compare: player top vs banker top, player bottom vs banker bottom. Both player hands win or one wins and one ties = player wins even money; one wins one loses = push; otherwise player loses. Banker wins ties.',
    Player: 'Players bet; each receives three tiles and arranges them in a line to form top and bottom hand (totals mod 10). Tiles placed face-down. Banker exposes three tiles and arranges similarly. Compare: player top vs banker top, player bottom vs banker bottom. Both player hands win or one wins and one ties = player wins even money; one wins one loses = push; otherwise player loses. Banker wins ties.',
    objective: "Form two hands (top and bottom) that respectively outrank the banker's two hands; baccarat-style scoring (pip total mod 10, nine high).",
    gameplay: 'Players bet; each receives three tiles and arranges them in a line to form top and bottom hand (totals mod 10). Tiles placed face-down. Banker exposes three tiles and arranges similarly. Compare: player top vs banker top, player bottom vs banker bottom. Both player hands win or one wins and one ties = player wins even money; one wins one loses = push; otherwise player loses. Banker wins ties.',
    keyRules: [
      'Three tiles each; arrange into top and bottom hand',
      'Scoring as Baccarat or Pai Gow: total each hand, drop tens digit; nine high, zero low',
      'If top outranks bottom by mistake, dealer may turn tiles 180 degrees',
      'Banker wins when both hands tie',
    ],
